# Binary artifacts, stored directly in git — NOT in LFS.
#
# LFS was removed 2026-09-05. The repo had drifted into a mixed state: 14 files were
# committed as raw bytes with the filter inactive (on a machine without git-lfs installed)
# while 11 were true pointers. On any machine where git-lfs IS active the clean filter
# rendered the first group as 130-byte pointers, so `git status` reported 14 permanent
# phantom modifications that no checkout could clear.
#
# These files are 22 KB-518 KB in a ~100 MB repo, so LFS bought nothing and cost a fetch
# dependency across two clones (laptop + AICR cluster) plus an HF Space remote. Converting
# to plain git added 3.40 MB and rewrote no history.
data/directions/*.npz -text
data/analysis/*.npz -text
data/analysis/figures/*.png -text
